  {
    "id": 3962984049,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "**Double free and dangling `char_sdesc` when `iedit` edits a corpse, the live object with no prototype this branch is for.**\n\n`copy_object_strings()` (`src/olc/genobj.c:556-570`) duplicates every string that `free_object_strings()` (`:469-487`) frees except `char_sdesc`. `make_corpse()` sets it (`src/combat/fight.c:2224`), and a corpse is an object with no prototype.\n\nRepro, as an immortal: `iedit corpse`, then `Q`.\n\n1. `iedit_setup_existing()` (`src/olc/oedit.c:4035`): `copy_object(edited, live)` -> `*edited = *live`, so `edited->char_sdesc == live->char_sdesc`.\n2. `iedit_commit_existing()` (`oedit.c:3994`): `copy_object(live, edited)` -> this line frees `live->char_sdesc`, then `*live = *edited` writes the freed pointer back into the corpse.\n3. `oedit.c:4021`: `free_object_strings(edited)` frees the same block again. The corpse keeps the dangling pointer: read by the vampire-spawn naming at `src/magic/magic.c:13334`, freed a third time when the corpse decays (`free_obj()` -> `free_object_strings()`).\n\nSecond trigger, same cause: a disconnect during the `iedit` (`close_socket()` -> `cleanup_olc()`, `src/olc/oasis.c:138`) frees `edited->char_sdesc`, which is the live corpse's.\n\nVerified under valgrind on `8556f9ca8` with a probe that mirrors the three calls on a `clear_object()`ed `live` with `char_sdesc = strdup(\"Rhiannon\")` and `obj_proto = NULL`:\n\n```c\ncopy_object(&edited, &live);   /* oedit.c:4035 */\ncopy_object(&live, &edited);   /* oedit.c:3994 */\nfree_object_strings(&edited);  /* oedit.c:4021 */\nCuAssertStrEquals(tc, \"Rhiannon\", live.char_sdesc);\n```\n\n`Invalid free()` at `free_object_strings (genobj.c:483)`, block already freed by `free_object_strings` from `copy_object (genobj.c:577)`, then `Invalid read` on `live.char_sdesc`.\n\nOn master the same path frees `char_sdesc` from `free_object_strings_proto()` after reading `obj_proto[-1]`. `a0757112c` removes the out-of-bounds read and keeps the double free, and `Test_gameplay_object_editor_copy_frees_an_object_with_no_prototype` does not set `char_sdesc`, so neither sanitizer job sees it.\n\nFix, one line in `copy_object_strings()` after the `arcane_mark` line (the probe is clean under valgrind with it):\n\n```c\nto->char_sdesc = from->char_sdesc ? strdup(from->char_sdesc) : NULL;\n```\n\nEvery copy that `copy_object_strings()` fills is later freed by `free_object_strings()` or `free_object_strings_proto()`, and both free `char_sdesc`, so the copy has to own it. Give the new test `source.char_sdesc` and `live.char_sdesc` of their own, assert `live.char_sdesc` equals the source text at a different address, and free both, so the memory-check and sanitizer jobs cover the path.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
