  {
    "id": 3962985437,
    "type": null,
    "body": "Adversarial review of `8556f9ca8`: one finding, the inline thread on `src/olc/genobj.c:577` (double free of a corpse's `char_sdesc` through `iedit`, with a verified one-line fix).\n\nChecked and clean: every source of an `arcane_mark` on an unnumbered object is a `strdup` (file and player-row loaders, `spell_arcane_mark()`, `copy_object_strings()`), no prototype carries one (`parse_object()` reads none, `oedit` sets none), no code strips a live object's prototype number after creation, and `delete_object()` extracts every instance before the table shrinks, so the new `free()` in `free_object_strings()` never meets a shared pointer. The two new tests are valgrind-clean on the head; the MR's `update_all_objects()` string sharing is #30 and not re-raised here.",
    "author": {
