    "id": 3963373829,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Confirmed and fixed in `ddacf712f`, the commit after the tag.\n\n- `copy_object_strings()` duplicates `char_sdesc`, the line as proposed. Every copy it fills is\n  freed by `free_object_strings()` or `free_object_strings_proto()`, and both free `char_sdesc`.\n- `Test_gameplay_object_editor_copy_frees_an_object_with_no_prototype` gives `source` and `live`\n  a `char_sdesc` of their own, asserts `live.char_sdesc` is the source's text at a different\n  address, and frees both. On `8556f9ca8` it fails on the shared pointer\n  (`live.char_sdesc == source.char_sdesc`), before the frees would meet one block.\n- With the fix: the two editor-copy tests and `Test_object_without_a_prototype_frees_its_arcane_mark`\n  are clean under valgrind; `make -j16 test` 2041 pass; `scripts/ci/local/run.py --base gitlab/master`\n  33 of 33 jobs pass (281 s).\n\nPhase 7 (`584524ec5`, MR !26) had met the same double free through the `iedit` commit and carries\nthe same line; its branch now has this commit merged in, so the two merge requests share one copy\nof it and !26 merges cleanly after !25.",
